{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017weWKCpRkjUg7ME2SgugKV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings, plain-markdown source of truth).\n\n- **Core purpose â€” a task/project manager over markdown.** It reads and writes plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`) as the single source of truth â€” no database, no lock files. Tasks move through a lifecycle: Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, each with optional notes.\n\n- **What it ships â€” a self-contained local web app.** The declared deliverable is `anchor_gui.py`: a Python-stdlib-only HTTP server that generates the full interactive dashboard HTML on every request and binds `http://localhost:8777`. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` (auto-start) on the host `PUTER`/`gwl-server`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same operations and emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **A layered \"R&D control surface\" for trio-driven development.** On top of task management, Anchor has grown four versioned surfaces (v2 â†’ v4) that turn each project into a cockpit for the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** trio: per-lane sessions, cached/validated AI summaries, a \"Grass Catchers\" idea lane, and pinnable deliverables.\n\n- **v3 \"Mission Control\" + v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (built & merged to master).** Real interactive terminals run over Windows **ConPTY** (`pywinpty` â€” the *one* declared exception to the stdlib-only rule, lazily imported in `pty_manager.py`), each session isolated in its own git worktree + branch. The current v4 cockpit shows each lane (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) as a status-lit tile that expands an inline panel (summary on top, resizable xterm.js terminal below), with an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only), per-lane doc roles, and a project cost/tokens/time rollup.\n\n- **Self-maintaining.** A daily 5 AM healthcheck (`anchor_healthcheck.py`, Task Scheduler) parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces, and writes a dated report â€” surfacing a red dashboard banner on failure.\n\n- **Branding.** Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using the one vendored brand mark as favicon and masthead lockup.\n\nThese claims are grounded in the project's `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star/decision anchors; I didn't re-verify them against the live code this turn. Want me to spot-check any specific claim against the source?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e2f7e30-2ac4-4396-99ed-34ceff33268e","uuid":"174b3595-77db-4f79-a8e1-686e27ac26c8","request_id":"req_011Cc2HiYz5GazQdkCCt6wd4"}
